# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# morphcpu.pcf - pin constraints for iCE40UP5K-SG48
#
# !! CANDIDATE ASSIGNMENT - NOT YET LOCKED !!
#
# The pin numbers below are a starting point, not a verified mapping. They must
# be checked against the iCE40 UltraPlus family pinout (Lattice FPGA-DS-02008,
# SG48 pinout table) and then made to agree with the schematic, because these
# two have to match exactly or the board does nothing. The schematic is the
# thing that fixes them; this file follows it, not the other way round.
#
# Before layout, confirm each of the following:
#
#  1. CLOCK. clk must land on a global-buffer-capable (GBIN) pin, or nextpnr
#     will route the 12 MHz clock through general fabric and timing closure
#     gets much harder. Check which SG48 pins are GBIN in the pinout table.
#
#  2. SPI CONFIG PINS ARE RESERVED. The dedicated SPI configuration pins that
#     load the bitstream from the config flash at power-on must not be reused
#     for LEDs or UART. Reserve them in the schematic and leave them out here.
#     See the iCE40 Programming and Configuration technical note (FPGA-TN-02001).
#
#  3. RGB DRIVER PINS ARE SPECIAL. Three SG48 pins are the SB_RGBA_DRV
#     constant-current open-drain LED driver outputs. They are not ordinary
#     I/O and should not be used for the plain 16-LED grid unless you
#     instantiate the RGB driver primitive. Keep the grid off them.
#
#  4. VCCIO BANKING. Every pin used here must sit in a bank whose VCCIO is
#     tied to the right rail in the schematic. Mixed-bank assignments that
#     look fine in nextpnr will not work if VCCIO is not connected.
#
# Once verified, delete this header block and record the pin table in
# JOURNAL.md with the datasheet page it came from.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- clock ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 12 MHz crystal oscillator. MUST be a GBIN pin - verify before locking.
set_io -nowarn clk        35

# --- reset ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Momentary button to GND, external pull-up. Active low.
set_io -nowarn rst_n      10

# --- UART to FT231X ---------------------------------------------------------
# Named from the FPGA's point of view:
#   uart_rx_i  <- FT231X TXD   (host to board)
#   uart_tx_o  -> FT231X RXD   (board to host)
set_io -nowarn uart_rx_i   6
set_io -nowarn uart_tx_o   9

# --- 16 LED grid ------------------------------------------------------------
# Cell index maps to the physical 4x4 grid, cell 0 top-left, row-major:
#
#     led[0]  led[1]  led[2]  led[3]      <- row 0
#     led[4]  led[5]  led[6]  led[7]      <- row 1
#     led[8]  led[9]  led[10] led[11]     <- row 2
#     led[12] led[13] led[14] led[15]     <- row 3
#
# The PCB silkscreen and the LED placement must follow this same order or the
# ripple will look scrambled. This mapping is the one thing that has to stay
# consistent across gateware, schematic and layout.
set_io -nowarn led[0]      2
set_io -nowarn led[1]      3
set_io -nowarn led[2]      4
set_io -nowarn led[3]     11
set_io -nowarn led[4]     12
set_io -nowarn led[5]     13
set_io -nowarn led[6]     18
set_io -nowarn led[7]     19
set_io -nowarn led[8]     20
set_io -nowarn led[9]     21
set_io -nowarn led[10]    23
set_io -nowarn led[11]    25
set_io -nowarn led[12]    26
set_io -nowarn led[13]    27
set_io -nowarn led[14]    28
set_io -nowarn led[15]    31
